# Short-Form Content Pipeline — environment template.
# Copy to ".env" and fill in. NEVER paste keys into the Claude chat — only into this file.

# DEFAULT transcription = FREE LOCAL WHISPER (on-device, no API key, no cost).
# This is a talking-head short-form video editor: video-use only TRANSCRIBES your
# recording (word-level timestamps) — it never generates audio. So NO key is needed
# by default. Leave everything below blank to use local Whisper.

# OPTIONAL alternative: ElevenLabs Scribe (hosted transcription).
# Only set this if you deliberately opt into ElevenLabs instead of local Whisper.
# Get one at https://elevenlabs.io/app/settings/api-keys
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL alternative: OpenAI Whisper API (hosted, PAID per-minute — not free).
# Only set this if you deliberately opt into OpenAI instead of local Whisper.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Note: the default free local-Whisper path needs NO key (see README "Transcription options").

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLISHING (the /postprocess skill) — optional, only if you publish via Metricool.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Metricool itself needs NO key here: on the free plan we schedule through the
# Metricool MCP (remote, OAuth in the browser) — add the server once:
#   https://ai.metricool.com/mcp   (works on any plan; authorize your brand)
#
# Cloudflare R2 = where the finished MP4 is hosted so Metricool can fetch it
# (the free MCP can't upload local files; `media` must be a public URL).
# Setup once at https://dash.cloudflare.com → R2:
#   1. Create a bucket (default name here: shorts).
#   2. Enable its "Public Development URL" (gives a https://pub-XXXX.r2.dev base) OR a custom domain.
#   3. Create an R2 API token (Object Read & Write) → Access Key ID + Secret Access Key.
#   4. Your account id is in the R2 dashboard URL / endpoint.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=YOUR_ACCOUNT_ID
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=YOUR_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=YOUR_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY   # keep private
# R2_BUCKET=shorts
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://pub-XXXXXXXX.r2.dev    # the bucket's public base, no trailing slash

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI REEL COVERS (/postprocess §3b) — optional, only if you generate AI covers.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Covers are generated with nano-banana (Gemini CLI extension), NOT an MCP.
# One-time setup:
#   1. Install the CLI + extension:  gemini extensions install \
#        https://github.com/gemini-cli-extensions/nanobanana
#   2. Get a Gemini API key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   3. Set GEMINI_API_KEY (below, or as a user/OS env var).
# The recurring avatar base + canonical prompts live in vault/Conceptos/visual_identity.md.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY   # keep private

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMMENT→DM FUNNELS (/funnel) — optional, only for zero-touch trigger creation.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Zernio (zernio.com) is a Meta Business Partner: it creates the comment→DM keyword
# trigger via API (POST /v1/comment-automations), so /funnel can go live without
# pasting into a dashboard. First 2 connected accounts are FREE.
# Setup once: sign up → connect your IG (OAuth) → create an API key.
# Then fill the three values (get profile/account ids via GET /api/v1/profiles and
# /api/v1/accounts, or let the /funnel script resolve them for you).
# ZERNIO_API_KEY=sk_...              # keep private
# ZERNIO_PROFILE_ID=
# ZERNIO_ACCOUNT_ID=
